// Title: Is Traffic Analytics data arriving? Records per hour and per table
// Purpose: Check ingestion before you trust (or blame) a flow query: how many records per bin, last record,
//          and which Traffic Analytics tables exist.
// Source table(s): AzureNetworkAnalytics_CL, NTANetAnalytics, NTAIpDetails
// Parameters to edit: Lookback.
// Notes/traps: after re-pointing flow logs to another workspace or re-enabling Traffic Analytics the data
//          gap can last an hour or more. NTA* tables are the new schema, AzureNetworkAnalytics_CL is the
//          legacy custom log, both can exist side by side. `evaluate narrow()` shows one row's
//          columns, handy to learn the schema.
//
// --- Query 1: records per table
let Lookback = 6h;
union isfuzzy=true AzureNetworkAnalytics_CL, NTANetAnalytics, NTAIpDetails
| where TimeGenerated > ago(Lookback)
| summarize records = count(), lastRecord = max(TimeGenerated) by Type
//
// --- Query 2: records per hour for the legacy table (run separately)
// AzureNetworkAnalytics_CL
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(6h)
// | summarize Records = count(), Last = max(TimeGenerated) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)
// | order by TimeGenerated desc
//
// --- Query 3: one NTAIpDetails row with all columns (run separately)
// NTAIpDetails | where TimeGenerated > ago(2h) | take 1 | evaluate narrow() | project Column, Value
